TIP:  This is patterned after Nanci’s studio version but I’ve included the link to her live version because it so epitomizes her stage presence and is a joy to listen to.  Kathy combines the first two verses before singing the chorus.

TIP:  (Asus2) will always follow and (A) so just lift off the bottom finger.  And (D/A) is just (D) with your pinky added to the the 4th string/4th fret to cover that middle <f#>.  If the (D/A) is too cumbersome you can play a (Bm) wherever you see the (D/A).

TIP:  Nanci drags the last syllable in the chorus.  So hold the (A) and (D/A) on “now,” “me” and “dime” and play it on the back end of the word.  It’s subtle but you’ll see what I mean when you get there.


